    <h1>Automotive accessories worth researching first</h1>
    <p class="lead">Choose accessories that solve a real driving problem. Vehicle compatibility, safe installation, and useful features matter more than an impressive specification on the box.</p>
    <h2>Portable jump starters</h2>
    <p>Match the starter to your vehicle's battery voltage and engine size. The NOCO GB40 is rated for 12V lead-acid batteries and gas engines up to 6.0L or diesel engines up to 3.0L. Recharge and maintain it according to the manufacturer's instructions; it is an emergency starting aid, not a replacement for repairing a failing battery.</p>
    <p><a href="https://no.co/gb40/specs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Review NOCO GB40 specifications →</a></p>
    <h2>Portable tire inflators</h2>
    <p>Look for an inflator that reaches all four tires, has a readable gauge, and works with your vehicle's available power source. The VIAIR 88P connects using battery clamps, rather than an ordinary 12V accessory socket. Check the vehicle manufacturer's recommended tire pressure on the door-jamb placard, not the maximum pressure printed on the tire sidewall.</p>
    <p><a href="https://viaircorp.com/products/88p-portable-compressor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Review VIAIR 88P specifications →</a></p>
    <h2>Dash cameras</h2>
    <p>Compare video resolution, field of view, storage, low-light performance, and the cost of optional cloud features. Garmin's Dash Cam Mini 3 records at 1080p with a 140-degree field of view and a built-in polarizer. Parking surveillance and remote features may require additional power equipment or subscriptions. Follow local laws and privacy requirements.</p>
    <p><a href="https://www.garmin.com/en-US/p/1223369/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Review Garmin Dash Cam Mini 3 specifications →</a></p>
    <h2>Other categories to compare</h2>
    <p>Car vacuums, interior organizers, phone mounts, charging accessories, and detailing supplies can make everyday driving easier. Check dimensions, materials, mounting stability, and whether a product obstructs airbags or visibility.</p>
